  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "number": "402-IV",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Mandatory Appendix 402-IV Installer Qualification"
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-1 INTRODUCTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(a) The repair of components using composite laminates differs considerably from other repair techniques and the quality of the installation depends strongly on satisfactory craftsmanship."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(1) Training and qualification of personnel are therefore key elements of a successful repair."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(2) This Appendix outlines the requirements for training, qualification, and approval of installers and supervisors/trainers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(b) Supervisors and trainers shall have the same qualification requirements but may hold different positions within the organization of the Repair System vendor."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-2 TRAINING"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(a) Courses and training shall be arranged by or with the assistance of the Repair System supplier."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(b) Training shall give a theoretical and practical introduction to the most important elements in the installation of the Repair System."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-2.1 Coursework (Installer)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(a) The course shall include training in:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(1) definition of a Repair System"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(2) terminology, types of repair"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(3) hazards associated with pressurized systems"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(4) health, safety, and environment"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(5) surface preparation"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(6) material preparation"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(7) material application"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(8) control of repair conditions"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(9) quality control"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(b) A written test covering the above subjects shall be taken and passed by the installer."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-2.2 Coursework (Supervisor/Trainer)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(a) The supervisor/trainer shall be a qualified installer. (b) The supervisor/trainer shall complete the following additional training:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(1) supervisor's/trainer's duties and responsibilities"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(2) evaluation methods used in repair design"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(3) health and safety"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(4) installation checklist and hold points"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(5) inspection of repairs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(c) A written test covering the above subjects shall be"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "taken and passed by the supervisor/trainer."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-2.3 Installer-Specific Qualification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(a) Installers shall be qualified for each specific Repair System through practical tests for Type A and/or Type B. (b) All specific approval tests shall be carried out in"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "accordance with relevant installation procedures."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "(c) Repair shall pass visual inspection completed in accordance with para. 402-5.2 witnessed by a supervisor or instructor."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-3 TRAINING RECORDS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "The employer of the Repair System installers and supervisors/trainers shall keep records of their training."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "402-IV-4 QUALIFICATION PERIOD"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 253,
      "text": "Theinstaller qualification shall remain valid for a period of 1 yr following the installation of the last successful repair."
    }
  ]
}